# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify (both read this file).
#
# Reqon is a single-page app: React Router handles /register,
# /board and the rest in the browser. The host only ever has one real file,
# index.html, so without this rule a direct visit to
# https://<site>/register — a refresh, a bookmark, a pasted link — asks the
# host for a /register file that does not exist and gets a 404.
#
# 200 (not 301/302) means "serve index.html but keep the URL", so React Router
# still sees /register and renders the right screen.
/*    /index.html   200
